# business-game

C++23 SFML engine and Arkanoid game. Code lives in `engine/` (`namespace eng`) and `games/arkanoid/` (`namespace arkanoid`, executable `arkanoid`). Contract: `docs/explanation/architecture.md`. Longer-term notes live in `mvp/` (`01`–`09` prospect, `10` living).

## Stack

- C++23, CMake ≥ 3.20, Ninja presets (`debug` / `release`)
- SFML 3.1 via FetchContent (`cmake/FetchSFML.cmake`) — Graphics/Window/System only; no manual SFML install
- GoogleTest 1.18 only in Debug; clang-format / clang-tidy at repo root

## Layout

- `engine/core/` — value types (`eng_core`)
- `engine/input/` — `InputEvent`, `ActionMap`, `InputState` (`eng_input`)
- `engine/scene/` — `SceneI`, `SceneStack`, `SceneRequest` (`eng_scene`)
- `engine/loop/` — `FixedStepLoop`, `App`, `PlatformI`, `ClockI` (`eng_loop`)
- `engine/render/` — `RenderQueue`, `RendererI` (`eng_render`)
- `engine/collision/` — sweep / reflect (`eng_collision`)
- `engine/resources/` — `ResourceCache` (`eng_resources`)
- `engine/sfml/` — SFML adapters (`eng_sfml`); only engine target that links SFML
- `games/arkanoid/sim/` — headless breakout (`arkanoid_sim`)
- `games/arkanoid/app/` — scenes, HUD, assets (`arkanoid_app`)
- `games/arkanoid/main.cpp` — executable `arkanoid`
- `resources/fonts/` — UI TTF (`ASSET_DIR`)
- `tests/engine/`, `tests/arkanoid/` — GoogleTest suites (Debug only)
- `tests/mocks/` — `ClockMock`, `PlatformMock`, `RendererMock`

## Build / test

```sh
cmake --preset debug
cmake --build --preset debug --target arkanoid
cmake --build --preset debug --target build_ut
ctest --preset debug
```

Binary: `build/<preset>/bin/arkanoid` (`.exe` on Windows).

## Agent pitfalls

- New `.cpp` files belong in that module’s own `CMakeLists.txt` (`engine/<module>/` or `games/arkanoid/<sim|app>/`)
- Only `engine/sfml` and `games/arkanoid/main.cpp` may include SFML; `arkanoid/sim` stays headless
- Tests are headless except `event_translate_test`, which links `SFML::Window` and does not open a window
- Interfaces use the `FooI` suffix (`SceneI`, `RendererI`, `PlatformI`, `ClockI`)
- Scenes must not `close()` the platform; quit is `QuitApp` / `closeRequested`
- Pause is `RequestPause` when top is `pausable`; overlay is `PauseScene` (`opaque` false)
- Menu cancel is `QuitApp`; overlay cancel is resume (`PopScene`)
- `SceneStack` applies push/pop/replace after the update walk
- Design notes: `mvp/01`–`09` (prospect). Tree names and slices: `mvp/10-engine-progress.md`
